# Moved from bootstrap/examples/family-bracket-leaf.moss. Verdicts below credited to the
# oracle are the old Rocq oracle's (moss_m2, removed when moss-ref replaced
# it), so they are historical; the suite checks the current verdicts.
# PublicFormation.FamilySigOk as first stated is false: Fam is a family
# (R.m's signature mentions no P(F) symbol), but its result leaf
# `Ctx[X = Foo]` carries Y into R.m's result type through the context's
# bracket. Applied at a matching Y := v that the demanded key R.m does not
# determine, R.m is provided at the ok receiver R with result Foo[Y = v],
# not ok for an arbitrary v. Elaboration reads the matching off the key
# (FamilyReadOff), under which the signature is ok, so the proof assumes
# that form (FamilySigReadOffOk, discharged by
# PublicFamilySig.family_sig_ok_readoff). Oracle and native accept this.
type R;
type X;
type Y;
assume Y { tag Foo(Y); }
assume X { fn R.m(): X; }
assume X { context Ctx = R.m; }
functor Fam[Y]: R, Y -> Ctx[X = Foo];
fn main() {}
